# Input graph for LA3D__cogitarelink-solid__tests_test_interop_foundation.py__test_one_manager_per_container_assigns_a_container_tree.
#
# The region asserts a chain of four invariants and RAISES if any fails
# (`assert x is not None, "..."`), so the only call this driver can make is
# one where every invariant already holds (see meta.json/translation_notes
# for why the zero-solution branch cannot be exercised through run_pair
# here). What the fixture CAN still do is prove the read patterns are
# scoped precisely, not just "anything matches":
#
#   * ex:mgr1 a st:Manager -- the ONE st:Manager-typed subject, so
#     `m{ ?mgr a st:Manager }.first()` is unambiguous (a second Manager
#     would make `.first()`'s pick non-deterministic between two valid
#     files' worth of content, which is not something a store promises).
#   * ex:mgr1 -> ex:assign1 -> (st:assigns, st:manages): the full chain,
#     exercising `.first()` reused for its value (assigns/manages both feed
#     later checks) and `bool(m{ })` for the pure existence check on
#     st:manages (the discarded-value read genuinely present in this
#     region -- see translation_notes).
#   * NEIGHBOURHOOD that must NOT match: ex:notAManager carries the same
#     st:hasAssignment edge as the real manager but is typed something
#     else, so it must not be picked up by `?mgr a st:Manager`; and
#     ex:decoyAssignment carries an unrelated st:manages triple, proving
#     `{a} st:manages ?x` is scoped to the assignment actually reached
#     (ex:assign1), not any st:manages triple anywhere in the graph.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix st: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shapetrees#> .

ex:mgr1 a st:Manager ;
    st:hasAssignment ex:assign1 .

ex:assign1 st:assigns <http://example.org/trees/WikiMemoryContainerTree> ;
    st:manages ex:container1 .

# Neighbourhood -- must not match.
ex:notAManager a ex:SomethingElse ;
    st:hasAssignment ex:assign1 .

ex:decoyAssignment st:manages ex:decoyContainer .
